{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337285-peach-leading-battle-groups-homebrow-mechanics-for-frontline-commanders","id":1337285,"title":"[PEACH] Leading Battle Groups : Homebrow Mechanics for frontline commanders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-21T19:11:06-07:00","id":1337285,"title":"[PEACH] Leading Battle Groups : Homebrow Mechanics for frontline commanders","content":"I'm looking to give combat-oriented commanders a way to combine with their battle group, becoming a sort of enhanced battle group like in the Lunar Charm Locust-and-Starling Legion.<br /> <br /> Here's what I got so far - Any critique is welcome, especially pointing out anything that would break with such a system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit : </i>changes are in green.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Leading Battle Groups</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> A Character with 3+ War who is in Close range of a battle group they can command\u00b9 may decide to Lead that battle group as a Simple action. This causes the battle group to lose its Initiative Track, becoming an extension of the Leader character. The Leader's Initiative is not inert - she may gain and lose Initiative as normal. In the unlikely event that the battle group's Initiative is negative at the time it joins with a Leader, the Leader loses the same amount of Initiative that the battle group is missing when she assumes leadership.<br /> <br /> The Leader is technically still the same combatant - any Movement or Combat actions she has used before assuming leadership remain spent after joining the battle group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3399ff\"><b>Attacking</b></span><br /> <br /> On her turn the Leader decides <span style=\"color:#008000\">whether she and the battle group act separately or together.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">If the Leader and the battle group choose to act separately, each gets a Combat action as usual and the Leader may issue a Command to the battle group as normal.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">When both act together, a battle group Leader may make a coordinated attack in place of a regular attack. A coordinated attack hits a main target and every target within close range of the main target. In the case of a ranged attack, the attack hits friend and foe alike. In either case, the rolls for a coordinated attack are resolved using the rules for swarming attacks<i>\u00b2</i> (single attack roll, gain initiative from the highest damage only, decisive attacks split initiative evenly). Coordinated attacks require the battle group to have compatible weaponry - a leader shooting a distant target with a bow may not make a coordinated attack with a battle group that doesn't have ranged weaponry.</span><br /> <br /> The Leader may supplement coordinated attacks with Charms as with her regular attacks, however Simple Attack Charms <span style=\"color:#008000\">and Grapples </span>may not be turned into coordinated attacks. <span style=\"color:#008000\">The Leader's coordinated attacks may benefit from the Command actions of other characters which can command the battle group, gaining the bonus dice as Charm dice.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3399ff\"><b>Defending</b></span><br /> <br /> The Leader has both her own health pool and the battle group's Magnitude - attackers must choose whether they wish to thin the battle group or to go for its Leader when they attack. The Leader may use defensive Charms as normal, but the battle group counts as a separate entity for the effect of Charms - an Exalt that turns her skin to stone only increases her own Defense, not that of her battle group.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">A Leader may reflexively redirect an attack against the battle group towards herself. To do this, the Leader must be within range of the attack (so she could not block an attack against the rear lines while at the front lines herself) and must be able to deflect the entire attack. Attacks that hit multiple targets normally cannot be intercepted by the Leader without Charms, although an appropriate stunt may allow it at the Storyteller's discretion.</span><br /> <br /> When a battle group loses a point of Size from having their Magnitude depleted, the Leader loses a portion of their Initiative equal to the portion of the army that has been wiped out (rounding up). For instance, if the battle group goes from Size 3 to Size 2, the Leader loses one third of their Initiative ; when it lowers again from 2 to 1, the Leader loses half of their Initiative; and when the battle group is defeated, the Leader immediately goes into crash. If the Leader is already crashed, they do not lose further Initiative. Killing a battle group Leader immediately causes a Rout check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3399ff\"><b>Movement</b></span><br /> <br /> The battle group and its Leader move together and are considered to be in Close range of each other at all times. In truly large battle groups, a Leader may choose to hide within the battle group, putting distance between her and the battle group's front. This puts range bands between her and enemies, making her only vulnerable to ranged attacks, but also unable to use Close range attacks herself. Usually, a Leader can hide within Short, Medium and Long range of Size 3, 4 and 5 battle groups respectively.<span style=\"color:#008000\"> A Leader can move within the battle group once per turn as a reflexive Movement action. Further movement in the same turn will require her to use her Movement action as normal.</span><br /> <br /> A Leader and her battle group may separate <span style=\"color:#008000\">as a Miscellaneous action which does not take their Combat action for the turn</span>. This resets the Initiative of the Leader to its base value if it is above that value, and causes the battle group to regain an Initiative Track which starts at its base value. If this is done after using a coordinated attack, the Leader and the battle group are both considered to have used their Combat action for the turn. <span style=\"color:#008000\">If the leader moves or is moved outside of the battle group, the two separate automatically. </span>If either the battle group or its Leader is defeated, the remaining combatant is separated following the same rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3399ff\"><b>An Expandable System</b></span><br /> <br /> This sets up a base system from which a new line of War Charms can be created - for instance, a War Charm could redirect withering damage from the Magnitude to the Initiative track or vice versa; allow Leaders and battle groups to join or separate reflexively or with reduced penalties; cause a Rout check by crashing an enemy Leader; etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <i>\u00b9 commanding battle groups</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core p.209</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To issue a command action, a character must be either the recognized leader of a battle group\u2014such as the boss of a gang or the commander of an army\u2014or must be a known hero to the members of the group, whom they would be willing to trust and rally around in the midst of battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>\u00b2 swarming attacks</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunars Preview p.247</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarming attacks apply to all enemies within close range, using one attack roll. On withering attacks, only the highest damage roll awards Initiative. On decisive attacks, she divides her Initiative evenly among all hit enemies (rounding up) to determine the damage rolled against them. On gambits, she likewise divides her Initiative evenly among hit enemies (rounding up) for Initiative rolls, though she need only pay the gambit\u2019s Initiative cost once.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>EDIT : </i>It appears thread titles can't be edited. This shall therefore remain a homebrow thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-22-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T00:14:35-07:00","id":1337298,"title":"","content":"Let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> If I turn my skin to stone, then only my Soak is increased and the battlegroup remains vulnerable.<br /> <br /> If I set my sword on fire, then I can make a swarming attack with my single flaming sword on every character within Close range.<br /> <br /> Leading a battlegroup limits what Charms I can use, means I now lose Initiative when my squishy mortal troops die, I can no longer Throw/Slam, the battlegroup becomes easier to rout, I give up an action to take command, and the battlegroup loses its attack each round (because why wouldn't I rather attack with my own stats).<br /> <br /> Can you walk me through this? Is this just meant as a way to get Swarming attacks and Grapple with Melee?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T03:14:28-07:00","id":1337307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337285-peach-leading-battle-groups-homebrow-mechanics-for-frontline-commanders?p=1337298#post1337298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me get this straight.<br /> <br /> If I turn my skin to stone, then only my Soak is increased and the battlegroup remains vulnerable.<br /> <br /> If I set my sword on fire, then I can make a swarming attack with my single flaming sword on every character within Close range.<br /> <br /> Leading a battlegroup limits what Charms I can use, means I now lose Initiative when my squishy mortal troops die, I can no longer Throw/Slam, the battlegroup becomes easier to rout, I give up an action to take command, and the battlegroup loses its attack each round (because why wouldn't I rather attack with my own stats).<br /> <br /> Can you walk me through this? Is this just meant as a way to get Swarming attacks and Grapple with Melee?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for going through the whole thing.The concept is basically an exercise to convert the effect of Locust-and-Starling Legion into something anyone can use if they team up with a battle group. It's meant to buff a combat character rather than buff the battle group itself, and isn't meant to replace or outshine Command actions for a dedicated general (at least not without Charms).<br /> <br /> This is basically the Dawn leading a battle group to victory while the Zenith War Supernal oversees the entire battle from the back. (Now that I think about it, someone who leads a battle group should probably be able to benefit from Command actions, if only as a Charm bonus).<br /> <br /> Being unable to defend the battle group with your defensive Charms is a balance concern first and foremost. It forces the Exalt to invest in ways to defend the battle group such as Defend Other Charms. In the case of non-Exalt the leader is more of a bonus combatant that wouldn't even have been counted otherwise, so it's more about creating an opportunity to defeat a battle group by assassinating the leader.<br /> <br /> Right now Area Attacks are the only real benefit yeah, because they're just that strong in an Exalt's hands so I was wary of granting anything else in a baseline effect everyone gets (melee grapples is more of a side effect). If you think there should be more benefits / less drawbacks or that I've gotten something horribly wrong any feedback is welcome, this is very much a first draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-22-2019, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T06:30:00-07:00","id":1337320,"title":"","content":"Updated the system to make the mechanics less weird and grant combined units a bit more punch. I've put the changes in green so it's easier to see what changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T05:26:56-07:00","id":1337478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337285-peach-leading-battle-groups-homebrow-mechanics-for-frontline-commanders?p=1337307#post1337307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wary of granting anything else in a baseline effect everyone gets (melee grapples is more of a side effect). If you think there should be more benefits / less drawbacks or that I've gotten something horribly wrong any feedback is welcome, this is very much a first draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checking I understood. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1337285-peach-leading-battle-groups-homebrow-mechanics-for-frontline-commanders?p=1337320#post1337320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated the system to make the mechanics less weird and grant combined units a bit more punch. I've put the changes in green so it's easier to see what changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see more value in this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}